xwayland: give X11 apps the real pixels at fractional scales

Stock mutter rounds the Xwayland scale up to a whole number (ceil of the highest monitor scale), so at
150% on a 3840x2160 monitor X11 apps (every Proton game) get a 5120x2880 screen that is then shrunk,
and at 125% on 1920x1200 a 3072x1920 one. This uses the exact scale instead: X11 coordinates are
stage coordinates times 1.5, so X11 sees 3840x2160 and its windows are drawn 1:1, like KDE's
"apps scale themselves". The buffer scale of Xwayland surfaces becomes a float for that; regions are
scaled with a matrix when the scale isn't whole. The scale X11 toolkits use for themselves (GDK_SCALE,
Xft.dpi) is rounded down to a whole number, so they draw at 1x real pixels.

the-script (pkg/build-patched.sh) applies this to Arch's mutter.

